## Interface: 120100
## Title: DandersFrames |cff9482c9Options|r
## Notes: Settings panel, editors and debug tools for DandersFrames. Loads on demand.
## Author: Danders
## Version: v5.4.0-alpha.4
## Category: Danders
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\DandersFrames\Media\DF_Icon
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## RequiredDeps: DandersFrames
## AllowAddOnTableAccess: 1

# ============================================================
# DandersFrames Options -- load-on-demand companion
# ============================================================
# Everything the settings panel needs and the frames do not. Not loaded at
# login; DandersFrames loads it the first time you open /df.
#
# Measured on the PTR build: while this stays unloaded DandersFrames uses
# 9,192 KB instead of 12,348 KB -- 3,156 KB less, about 25% -- and ~59,000 lines
# are never parsed at any login. The memory saving lasts until the panel is
# opened; the parse saving happens every login regardless.
#
# RequiredDeps plus the matching name prefix makes the addon list show this
# as a collapsible child of DandersFrames rather than a separate entry.
#
# ☠ ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING in ONE place here, not three. Verified by resolving
# every file-scope alias in both addons rather than assumed -- two of the three
# constraints previously listed were not real, which is worse than none: a
# reader trusts the wrong ones and misses the one that bites.
#
#   REAL, and cross-addon: GUI/Pages/AutoProfiles.lua aliases the RESIDENT
#     AutoProfilesUI._priv (DandersFrames/Core/AutoProfiles.lua). The parent
#     addon always loads first, so this holds -- but it is the actual dependency.
#   REAL, within this addon: AuraDesigner/UI/Options.lua creates _uiState and
#     _priv; Groups -> Indicators -> Cards -> Editor alias them in that order.
#
#   NOT real: GUI/Sections -> Controls -> Panel. All three alias only
#     GUI._state / GUI._priv from the RESIDENT GUI.lua and Widgets.lua, never
#     each other. Reordering them breaks nothing.
#   NOT real: GUI/Pages/Options "first". The parts are a runtime tail-call
#     chain (_SetupGUIPagesPart2..5) -- each need only be loaded before
#     SetupGUIPages is CALLED, so TOC order among them is free.

# Selective import/export category tables. Only Profile.lua's selective
# paths and the Modules page read these; both load this addon first.
Core\ExportCategories.lua

# Changelog text (~180 KB string, GENERATED from CHANGELOG.md). Only the panel
# reads it, so it rides the companion; the stamped header stays resident.
Changelog.lua

# GUI parts used only by settings pages
# /dficons dev icon browser. Its slash registers on load; the /df debug
# dispatcher loads the companion on an unknown word, so first use still works.
GUI\IconLib.lua
# The load-on-demand half of the embedded DandersUI lib. This addon needs its
# OWN Libs\DandersUI copy -- a TOC cannot reference another addon's folder --
# and this manifest must load before the GUI files below, which call the
# surfaces it brings in.
Libs\DandersUI\DandersUI_Options.xml
# Widget factories the live addon never calls, lifted out of the resident
# GUI.lua / Widgets.lua. Loads first: the parts below build pages with them.
GUI\SettingsWidgets.lua
# Settings search. It has no entry point of its own -- the search bar is built
# by GUI\Panel.lua -- so it is only ever reachable with this addon loaded.
Features\Search.lua
# The changed-settings ledger. AFTER Search.lua (it reads DF.Search's registry
# at build time) and before the pages, one of which reads its PAGE_ID at file
# scope to name its own tab.
Features\ChangedSettings.lua
GUI\Sections.lua
GUI\Controls.lua
# The shared shell both designer pages are built on -- banner, canvas, strips,
# tab strip, then the active tab, all as bands in the harness's own column.
# AFTER Controls.lua (it is handed that file's CreatePopoutPageTools table) and
# before the designers, which call it.
GUI\DesignerShell.lua
GUI\Panel.lua
GUI\ColorPicker.lua
# The write half of the popout footer's group verbs (Reset Group / Hold:
# Defaults). Before the pages, which call it; it reads DF.Defaults at call time
# only, so nothing else about its position is load-bearing.
GUI\GroupActions.lua

# Settings pages -- Options.lua heads the chain, the rest follow in order
GUI\Pages\Options.lua
GUI\Pages\Frames.lua
GUI\Pages\Auras.lua
GUI\Pages\Indicators.lua
GUI\Pages\Modules.lua
GUI\Pages\AutoProfiles.lua
GUI\Pages\NicknamesPage.lua
GUI\Pages\NicknamesPicker.lua

# Aura Designer editor (migrations stay resident in the main addon)
AuraDesigner\UI\Options.lua
AuraDesigner\UI\Groups.lua
AuraDesigner\UI\Indicators.lua
AuraDesigner\UI\Cards.lua
# The popout layout's page (bands and rows). AFTER Cards.lua, whose helpers it
# aliases at load; BEFORE Editor.lua, which calls S.BuildPoolStrip from here.
AuraDesigner\UI\Rows.lua
AuraDesigner\UI\Editor.lua

# Text Designer editor
TextDesigner\UI\Options.lua
# The popout layout's page (bands and rows). AFTER Options.lua, whose private
# table it aliases at load, and AFTER AuraDesigner\UI\Cards.lua, whose frame
# canvas it borrows (designer rework decision 4 -- one description of the frame's
# anatomy, not two).
TextDesigner\UI\Rows.lua

# Filter Registry UI
FilterRegistry\UI\Options.lua
FilterRegistry\UI\SpellPicker.lua

# Click-Casting UI
ClickCasting\UI\Main.lua
ClickCasting\UI\ProfilesPanel.lua
ClickCasting\UI\BindingEditor.lua
ClickCasting\UI\Dialogs.lua

# Test mode -- TestMode\Shim.lua stays resident so live rendering always has
# the entry points; these overwrite the stubs when this addon loads.
TestMode\TestFramePool.lua
TestMode\TestMode.lua
# After TestMode.lua: it reads the frame pools that file owns.
TestMode\Labels.lua

# Debug tools (DebugConsole and Profiler stay resident in the main addon)
Debug\AuraExplorer.lua
Debug\AtlasBrowser.lua
Debug\MemoryTest.lua
# Profiler window; engine and SetScript hook stay resident in Debug/Profiler.lua
Debug\ProfilerUI.lua
Debug\AttachmentScan.lua
# Permanent workbench for the DandersUI popout look (/df popoutdemo). Plain lib
# widgets over a throwaway table -- no settings page is involved.
GUI\PopoutDemo.lua
